478 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Education: Access, Challenges, and Opportunities)
/E (Education: Access, Challenges, and Opportunities)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
479 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Education is a fundamental right, but in Dzaleka, access to quality education is severely limited. The camp has several primary and secondary schools, but these are often overcrowded, under-resourced, and staffed by volunteer teachers with limited training. The limited availability of secondary education, in particular, poses significant challenges for young people in the camp, many of whom are unable to continue their studies beyond the primary level.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
480 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The lack of access to higher education is another significant barrier, with very few opportunities for refugees to pursue tertiary education. Some organizations offer scholarships and distance learning programs, but these are limited and highly competitive.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
481 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Food security is a major concern in Dzaleka. The World Food Programme \(WFP\) provides monthly food rations to refugees, but these rations \(equivalent to USD 7.50 per person per month\) are insufficient to meet the nutritional needs of the population. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The situation is exacerbated by the lack of access to land for farming and the restrictions on employment, which limit refugees' ability to supplement their rations with other sources of food.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Malnutrition, particularly among children and pregnant women, is a significant problem in the camp. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The limited availability of diverse and nutritious foods contributes to high rates of anemia and other nutrition-related health issues.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Food Security and Nutritional Concerns)
/E (Food Security and Nutritional Concerns)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Shelter: Living Conditions in the Camp)
/E (Shelter: Living Conditions in the Camp)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Living conditions in Dzaleka are challenging, with overcrowding, inadequate housing, and limited access to basic amenities. Many refugees live in makeshift shelters constructed from mud, plastic sheeting, and other materials that offer little protection from the elements. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (While some organizations have provided materials and support for building more durable shelters, the demand far exceeds the supply, leaving many refugees in substandard housing.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
